<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title>BREAKING: Ole Miss star Kewan Lacy not expected to play vs. Florida</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>Pete Golding told ESPN the All-American running back has a left shoulder injury. Here's who replaces him before kickoff at 3:30 p.m. ET.</mj-preview>
    <mj-font name="Newsreader" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,600;6..72,700&amp;display=swap" />
    <mj-font name="Inter" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=swap" />
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="Inter, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text color="#14243D" font-size="16px" line-height="1.55" />
      <mj-button background-color="#FA4616" color="#FFFFFF" border-radius="0" inner-padding="14px 22px" font-size="13px" font-weight="800" />
    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-style>
      .gb-wordmark { font-weight:900; letter-spacing:-1.8px; }
      .gb-h1 { font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; font-size:36px; line-height:1.06; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-.5px; }
      .gb-quote { font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; font-size:22px; line-height:1.3; font-style:italic; }
      @media only screen and (max-width:480px) {
        .gb-h1 { font-size:29px !important; line-height:1.1 !important; }
        .gb-quote { font-size:19px !important; }
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#F2F0EB" width="640px">

    <!-- Breaking bar -->
    <mj-section background-color="#FA4616" padding="10px 24px">
      <mj-column width="60%">
        <mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="13px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="3px" padding="0">BREAKING NEWS</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column width="40%">
        <mj-text align="right" color="#FFFFFF" font-size="11px" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1px" padding="1px 0 0">SAT., SEPT. 26</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Masthead -->
    <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="16px 24px 12px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/?utm_source=gatorbait_breaking_email&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=breaking_lacy_2026_09_26&amp;utm_content=masthead" style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="gb-wordmark" style="font-size:32px;color:#003B7A;">GATOR</span><span class="gb-wordmark" style="font-size:32px;color:#FA4616;">BAIT</span></a><br/>
          <span style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:3px;color:#003B7A;">MEDIA</span>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Cover -->
    <mj-section background-color="#081B35" padding="0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_bacb6e6384e3433f89699b53cbee3f90~mv2.png" alt="Breaking: Ole Miss running back Kewan Lacy is not expected to play against Florida." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/kewan-lacy-not-expected-to-play-ole-miss-florida?utm_source=gatorbait_breaking_email&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=breaking_lacy_2026_09_26&amp;utm_content=cover_image" padding="0" width="640px" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Story -->
    <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="26px 30px 6px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 14px" color="#081B35"><span class="gb-h1">Ole Miss star RB Kewan Lacy not expected to play vs. Florida</span></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 14px">No. 4 Ole Miss is expected to be without its most dangerous runner in The Swamp. Lacy, a 2025 All-American, is not expected to play against No. 21 Florida because of a left shoulder injury, Rebels coach Pete Golding told ESPN&rsquo;s Pete Thamel on Saturday.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 30px 8px">
      <mj-column border-left="5px solid #FA4616" padding="4px 0 4px 16px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 6px" color="#081B35"><span class="gb-quote">&ldquo;We still have another chapel session, so I&rsquo;m not giving up yet.&rdquo;</span></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0" font-size="12px" font-weight="800" letter-spacing="1.2px" color="#5F6B7A">PETE GOLDING TO ESPN</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- What we know -->
    <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="18px 30px 4px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px" color="#D8450C" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px">WHAT WE KNOW</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 12px"><strong>The injury:</strong> Lacy hurt his left shoulder in last week&rsquo;s 32-24 win over then-No. 7 LSU, leaving in the third quarter after 43 yards and a touchdown on nine carries. He had X-rays after the game and an MRI on Sunday, and was downgraded to doubtful on Friday&rsquo;s SEC injury report.</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 12px"><strong>Who replaces him:</strong> JT Lindsey (No. 26), a sophomore who transferred from LSU, and Makhi Frazier (No. 25), a junior transfer from Michigan State, will split the carries, ESPN reported. Lindsey has 48 yards on 12 carries this season; Frazier has 38 yards on nine.</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 12px"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Lacy set Ole Miss single-season records last year with 306 carries, 1,567 yards and 24 rushing touchdowns and was a Doak Walker Award finalist alongside Florida&rsquo;s Jadan Baugh. This season he has 191 yards and four touchdowns on 39 carries.</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 12px"><strong>The history:</strong> Florida knows him well. Last Nov. 15, Lacy ran for 224 yards and three touchdowns in Ole Miss&rsquo; 34-24 win over the Gators in Oxford, breaking the school&rsquo;s single-season rushing touchdown record that day.</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 16px"><strong>Florida&rsquo;s own watch:</strong> Wide receiver Eric Singleton Jr. (sprained left ankle) is a game-time decision, though coach Jon Sumrall told ESPN he feels decent about his chances.</mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/kewan-lacy-not-expected-to-play-ole-miss-florida?utm_source=gatorbait_breaking_email&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=breaking_lacy_2026_09_26&amp;utm_content=read_full_story" align="left" padding="0 0 26px">READ THE FULL STORY</mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Kickoff -->
    <mj-section background-color="#081B35" padding="22px 30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text color="#FA7A45" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 6px">KICKOFF</mj-text>
        <mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.35" font-weight="800" padding="0 0 6px">No. 4 Ole Miss (3-0) at No. 21 Florida (3-0)</mj-text>
        <mj-text color="#D5DFEC" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 14px">3:30 p.m. ET on ABC from Ben Hill Griffin Stadium. Buddy Martin, Franz Beard and Loren Meadows are in The Swamp, with photographer Chris Spears. Look up any player&rsquo;s number and follow along on our homepage.</mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/?utm_source=gatorbait_breaking_email&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=breaking_lacy_2026_09_26&amp;utm_content=gameday_homepage" align="left" padding="0" background-color="#FFFFFF" color="#081B35">ROSTERS &amp; GAME DAY UPDATES</mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="18px 26px 22px">
      <mj-column width="40%">
        <mj-text padding="0" color="#003B7A" font-size="18px" font-weight="900">GATOR<span style="color:#FA4616;">BAIT</span> MEDIA</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column width="60%">
        <mj-text align="right" color="#667386" font-size="11px" line-height="1.55" padding="0">Florida football. All the time.<br/>Information from ESPN, Field Level Media and Ole Miss Athletics was used in this report.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
